      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Asymmetric copper-catalyzed intermolecular amino- and azidocyanation reactions of alkenes have been developed that proceed via a radical process in which a key benzylic radical intermediate is enantioselectively trapped by a chiral Box/CuII cyanide complex. A variety of enantiomerically enriched β-amino/azido alkylnitriles were efficiently synthesized. The β-azido alkylnitriles could be converted into a series of highly valuable optically active amine-based building blocks and bioactive compounds."
      },
